{"id": 10008726, "reference": "A12/00903/23", "publication_date": "2023-04-27T10:07:50.542Z", "modification_date": "2023-04-27T10:07:50.545Z", "country": "Sweden", "product_category": "ELECTRICAL_APPLIANCES", "product_name": "Children's camera ", "product_name_specific": "Children's digital camera", "risk_description": "The plastic in a charger cable has an excessive concentration of bis(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate (DEHP) (measured value up to 1.14% by weight). The product also has an excessive concentration of short chain chlorinated paraffins (SCCPs) (measured value up to 3.59 % by weight).\nDEHP may harm the health by possibly possible damage to the reproductive system. SCCPs persist in the environment, are toxic to aquatic organisms at low concentrations and bio-accumulate in wildlife and humans, posing a risk to human health and the environment. Prolonged exposure to them through the skin may cause cancer. \n", "legal_provision": "The product does not comply with the requirements of the Directive on the restriction of the use of certain hazardous substances in electrical and electronic equipment (RoHS 2 Directive) nor comply with the Persistent Organic Pollutants (POP) Regulation.", "country_of_origin": "People's Republic of China", "sold_online": "YES", "notification_type": "ARTICLE_12", "brands": [], "model_types": [], "risk_types": ["CHEMICAL", "ENVIRONMENT"], "measures": ["PRODUCT_WITHDRAWAL_FROM_MARKET"], "embedding_model": "siglip2-b16-256", "embedding_dim": 768, "photos": [{"photo_id": 10079575, "main": true, "embedding": ""}, {"photo_id": 10079576, "main": false, "embedding": ""}, {"photo_id": 10079577, "main": false, "embedding": ""}]}